  "body": "Given the examples `new URL('file:///C%3A/a/b/c')` and `new URL('file:///C%7C/a/b/c')`, the parsed pathnames do not unescape the `%3A` (`:`) and `%7C` (`|`). Technically speaking, those should be considered valid Windows drive letters. Currently neither the Node.js, Firefox, or Chrome impls decode the %-encoded `:` and `|` characters.",
